getsectsize.c defines BLKSSZGET and BLKPBSZGET itself, but only when _IO is
already defined, and it gets <sys/ioctl.h> (and with it _IO) only together
with <linux/fd.h>.  The libc has no floppy header, so without this the
logical and physical sector size queries compiled to "unknown" and mke2fs
took every device for a 512-byte one -- wrong on 4096-byte NVMe namespaces.

